Commit 1a73dc590cbad62d6f0329ea4779eadaa8d8fd75 of OpenSSL's openssl-3.5
branch, which fixes CVE-2026-88822. The QUIC stack detects the peer
address of a connected socket with BIO_CTRL_DGRAM_DETECT_PEER_ADDR,
which sizes the buffer for getpeername() by a struct sockaddr, 16 bytes,
too few for IPv6's 28, and returns the bytes of the address beyond those
getpeername() writes: stack bytes that were never initialized. The patch
zeroes the address and gives getpeername() its whole size. OpenSSL
3.5.10 holds the fix; 3.5.9 does not.

From: Neil Horman <nhorman@openssl.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:28:03 -0500
Subject: crypto/bio/bss_dgram.c: initialise variable in
 BIO_CTRL_DGRAM_DETECT_PEER_ADDR
---
 crypto/bio/bss_dgram.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crypto/bio/bss_dgram.c b/crypto/bio/bss_dgram.c
index 968104a..6511219 100644
--- a/crypto/bio/bss_dgram.c
+++ b/crypto/bio/bss_dgram.c
@@ -760,8 +760,8 @@ static long dgram_ctrl(BIO *b, int cmd, long num, void *ptr)
         BIO_ADDR_make(&data->peer, BIO_ADDR_sockaddr((BIO_ADDR *)ptr));
         break;
     case BIO_CTRL_DGRAM_DETECT_PEER_ADDR: {
-        BIO_ADDR xaddr, *p = &data->peer;
-        socklen_t xaddr_len = sizeof(xaddr.sa);
+        BIO_ADDR xaddr = { 0 }, *p = &data->peer;
+        socklen_t xaddr_len = sizeof(xaddr);
 
         if (BIO_ADDR_family(p) == AF_UNSPEC) {
             if (getpeername(b->num, (void *)&xaddr.sa, &xaddr_len) == 0
